<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!-- Access model (see CLAUDE.md > Permissions). Every permission is its own
         privilege with one "Allowed" group, whose record rules give it its
         meaning. They all imply the technical Inventory user group, which opens
         the app (with Odoo's Inventory User group, which holds the ACLs) and
         carries a deny rule per operation, so users can only do what a
         permission opens. Stock moves and move lines follow their transfer
         (moves outside a transfer, such as adjustments and manufacturing, stay
         open); cost analysis lines follow their analysis. "Own" transfers are
         the ones they created or are Responsible for; "My Team" adds those
         created by the people under them in the org chart.

         Cost analyses are part of Inventory: every internal user is denied
         them unless an Inventory permission opens them, so Product Cost
         Analysis' own open access rights don't reach past these rules.

         Workflow privileges: Transfers: Validate (checked in button_validate)
         and Inventory Adjustments: Apply (checked when counted quantities are
         applied). Users of Odoo's Inventory groups who have none of these
         permissions keep Inventory's own access. -->
